       <h1>Ben Affleck Labels Justice League Reshoots His Career's Low Point</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Ben Affleck described the reshoots for the film Justice League as the &quot;low point of my career&quot; during an appearance on the Happy Sad Confused podcast. The actor characterized the production process as &quot;gross&quot; following the studio's decision to replace director Zack Snyder with Joss Whedon.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/ben-affleck-labels-justice-league-reshoots-his-careers-low-p.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Warner Bros. initiated the overhaul after Snyder was forced to pause production due to the death of his daughter. The shift in direction significantly altered the project, leading to Affleck's public criticism of the circumstances surrounding the film's completion and the studio's management of the production.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and effectively summarizes the source material without padding.</p>
