     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-12 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>CPI(M) Calls Oct. 24 Hartal in Seven Pathanamthitta Villages Over ESA Notification</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The CPI(M) has announced a hartal on October 24 across seven villages in Pathanamthitta to demand their exclusion from the Centre's draft Ecologically Sensitive Area notification. District secretary Raju Abraham stated that finalized notifications would force residents to seek environmental approvals for farming and construction. Abraham criticized the State government for failing to seek the exclusion of any Pathanamthitta villages before the September 25 objection deadline. The protest targets Chittar, Seethathode, Aruvappulam, and Thannithode in Konni taluk, along with Vadasserikkara, Perunad, and Kollamula in Ranni taluk.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/cpim-calls-oct-24-hartal-in-seven-pathanamthitta-villages-ov.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise and accurately reflects the specific villages, the political context, and the reasoning behind the CPI(M) hartal as reported.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/cpim-calls-hartal-on-oct-24-in-7-pathanamthitta-villages-over-esa/article71574962.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
