       <h1>Ego Nwodim Criticizes Shane Gillis' SNL Monologue via Social Media</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Former &quot;Saturday Night Live&quot; cast member Ego Nwodim responded to host Shane Gillis' recent monologue regarding women's gym attire by sharing a gym photo of herself. Nwodim captioned the post &quot;Whore Reporting for Duty,&quot; appearing to shade Gillis' viral commentary on the gym habits of women.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/ego-nwodim-criticizes-shane-gillis-snl-monologue-via-social-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Gillis hosted last Saturday's episode of the sketch comedy show, where his opening monologue drew significant attention for jokes centered on women wearing scantily-clad outfits while exercising. The viral nature of the monologue prompted Nwodim's public response, which utilized her own workout image to address the comedian's controversial remarks.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the source's reporting on Nwodim's social media response to Gillis' SNL monologue.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/shane-gillis-snl-monologue-ego-nwodim-women-gym-1236909525/" rel="noopener">Variety</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
