       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-12 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Electric Car Insurance Claims Cost 14% More Than Petrol, Diesel Vehicles</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Personal Finance</span> <span>#EV</span> <span>#Insurance</span> <span>#Car Insurance</span></div>
       <p>Electric vehicle (EV) owners should be aware that insurance claims for repairs are, on average, 14% more expensive than those for comparable petrol and diesel cars. This trend indicates a higher financial outlay for EV repairs through insurance.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/electric-car-insurance-claims-cost-14-more-than-petrol-diese.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Moreover, these average costs are observed to rise further during monsoon conditions. This suggests that specific environmental factors can exacerbate repair expenses for electric vehicles, impacting overall insurance claim values.</p><p>This information, highlighted by Livemint Money, underscores a key difference in ownership costs for EVs compared to traditional internal combustion engine vehicles, particularly concerning insurance and repair expenses.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the core findings of the source summary and presents them clearly without unnecessary padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
