     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-12 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>IISER Tirupati-Melbourne University Tie-up Offers Dual Degrees</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#University</span> <span>#IISER</span> <span>#Australia</span></div>
       <p>A new academic collaboration between IISER Tirupati and Melbourne University has been announced, offering students the opportunity to earn two degrees. This tie-up enables students to 'Start in India, finish in Australia,' as reported by The Indian Express.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/iiser-tirupati-melbourne-university-tie-up-offers-dual-degre.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The partnership provides a pathway for students to commence their studies in India and complete their degree requirements in Australia, culminating in dual qualifications. This initiative aims to broaden educational horizons for students.</p><p>What to watch: Future announcements regarding program specifics from the universities.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source summary and provides a concise report of the collaboration.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
