       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-12 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>INMECC Calls for India to Capitalize on US Manpower Restrictions</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Indo Gulf and Middle East Chamber of Commerce (INMECC) stated that tightening United States manpower regulations provide India a unique opportunity to attract global technology and industrial investments. The organization is actively working to facilitate the establishment of foreign operational and technology centers within the country.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/inmecc-calls-for-india-to-capitalize-on-us-manpower-restrict.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>INMECC chairman N.M. Sharafudeen urged central and state governments, along with private-sector stakeholders, to act strategically to capture this emerging market shift. By positioning India as a preferred destination for international companies, the chamber aims to leverage the changing global business environment to bolster India's industrial and technological infrastructure.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the INMECC statement regarding US manpower regulations and the call for strategic investment in India.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/india-poised-to-woo-global-investments-amid-us-curbs-inmecc/article71575111.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
