     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-12 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by Crictracker, ESPN Cricinfo">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Jos Buttler Faces Lengthy Lay-off After Hamstring Surgery</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Jos Buttler</span> <span>#Injury</span> <span>#England Cricket</span></div>
       <p>England white-ball captain Jos Buttler underwent surgery on his left hamstring on October 12, 2026, and is now facing a lengthy lay-off, with no specific recovery timeline confirmed by the medical team, according to Crictracker. Buttler, aged 36, shared an update via an Instagram post on Monday, October 12, showing himself on a hospital bed with his left leg braced, giving a thumbs up. He captioned the post, &quot;Succesful surgery and on the road to recovery,&quot; adding, &quot;Feeling more motivated than ever!&quot; (Crictracker). ESPN Cricinfo also noted the former captain's motivation to return to fitness.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/jos-buttler-faces-lengthy-lay-off-after-hamstring-surgery.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The hamstring problem first emerged on September 24, 2026, when England played the second ODI against Sri Lanka at Headingley. Buttler, who had made 69 from 49 balls, hitting five sixes, left the field mid-innings after getting hurt but briefly returned to bat before the injury ended his involvement. This recurrence is understood to be a concern for the England medical staff, as a comparable injury to the same left hamstring had previously sidelined him during the 2024 IPL season. No official statement on the nature or extent of the surgical procedure has been released, Crictracker reported.</p><p>Buttler had already been withdrawn from England's tri-series assignment in Pakistan prior to the operation. The surgery now casts doubt over several further commitments in the coming months, including the Australia white-ball tour in November, for which the ECB was scheduled to name its squad on October 13, 2026. His franchise contract with Durban's Super Giants for the SA20, a competition commencing on January 17, 2027, is also uncertain given the lack of a recovery date.</p><p>Notably, on the same day as his operation, the ECB confirmed one-year contract extensions for both Buttler and leg-spinner Adil Rashid. Buttler’s revised deal will run out ahead of the 2027 50-over World Cup, scheduled to be held in South Africa. Before his injury, Buttler had been in consistent white-ball form, accumulating 466 runs across nine white-ball internationals after the T20 World Cup, a sequence that included his 69-run knock at Headingley. Earlier in 2026, he contributed 87 runs as England reached the T20 World Cup semi-final, and at domestic level, he captained Manchester Super Giants to The Hundred title, becoming the first male cricketer to reach 15,000 career T20 runs.</p><p>What to watch: Updates on Buttler's recovery and return to England's white-ball squad.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Excellent reporting that captures all key biographical, injury, and professional details from the source while maintaining a professional news tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/feeling-more-motivated-than-ever-jos-buttler-provides-update-after-hamstring-surgery-faces-lengthy-lay-off-9546/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1558191.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
