       <h1>Julia Child's Former Provence Home Operates as Culinary School</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>La Pitchoune, the former Provence home and kitchen of culinary icon Julia Child, continues to function as an active hub for cooking enthusiasts. The property has transitioned into a specialized cooking school and vacation rental, allowing guests to prepare meals in the original kitchen space.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/julia-childs-former-provence-home-operates-as-culinary-schoo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Held family, who acquired the residence in 2016, maintains the home to preserve Child's legacy and authentic atmosphere. Visitors are encouraged to recreate her classic dishes, with the school fostering a culinary environment designed to inspire students through the enduring spirit of Julia Child's work.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reflects the provided summary regarding the current use of Julia Child's former home.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
