     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-12 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kumar Kushagra Steps In for Injured Rishabh Pant in India A's New Zealand Tour</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India A</span> <span>#Rishabh Pant</span> <span>#Kumar Kushagra</span></div>
       <p>Wicket-keeper batter Rishabh Pant has been ruled out of the first two multi-day matches of India A's upcoming tour of New Zealand. Pant sustained a left-side strain while leading the Rest of India in the Irani Cup, prompting the Men's Selection Committee to name Kumar Kushagra as his replacement for these initial fixtures.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/kumar-kushagra-steps-in-for-injured-rishabh-pant-in-india-as.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The India A squad was originally announced on October 6, 2026, with Pant included. Following his injury, the BCCI confirmed that Kushagra will cover wicketkeeping duties for the opening two multi-day games. Dhruv Jurel will continue as captain of the India A side throughout the tour. The schedule for the three multi-day matches against New Zealand A includes the first from October 24 to 27 in Lincoln, the second from October 31 to November 3 in Christchurch, and the third from November 7 to 10 back in Lincoln.</p><p>Pant is currently under the care of the board's medical team and is reportedly recovering well, though no specific details regarding the severity of his left-side strain have been released. A decision on his availability for the third India A match, scheduled for November 7 to 10 in Lincoln, will be made at a later stage, leaving his participation in that fixture open.</p><p>Kumar Kushagra's inclusion ensures a like-for-like replacement for Pant, given his role as a wicketkeeper-batter. He joins the squad specifically for the Lincoln and Christchurch multi-day fixtures and is listed as the designated wicketkeeper for those two games. The rest of the India A squad remains as originally announced, featuring a blend of experienced domestic performers and younger talent, including Yashasvi Jaiswal, KL Rahul, and Washington Sundar.</p><p>What to watch: Pant's recovery and potential return for the final match.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately incorporates all relevant details from the source, including the specific dates, replacement personnel, and the status of the third match.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/kumar-kushagra-replaces-rishabh-pant-in-india-a-squad-for-new-zealand-tour-2523/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
