     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-12 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Riyadh Airport Attacked Again Following Deadly Strike</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh faced a new attack one day after a strike killed 12 people. While the Saudi-led coalition intercepted a cruise missile on Sunday, civil aviation authorities confirmed subsequent injuries from another strike. Iran-backed Houthi rebels have also claimed responsibility for attacks on Dammam airport and Aramco facilities, though Saudi officials have not confirmed these reports.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/riyadh-airport-attacked-again-following-deadly-strike.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The violence follows an escalation in hostilities after Saturday’s deadly airport strike. In response, airstrikes targeted Yemen’s Sanaa International Airport on Sunday, with Houthis blaming the Saudi-led coalition. The Houthis have issued fresh threats regarding Saudi airspace amid the ongoing conflict.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the reported events, though it relies on live-blog style reporting which can be inherently volatile.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/saudi-arabia-houthis-us-iran-war-live-updates-yemen-riyadh-airport-attack-strait-of-hormuz-uae-middle-east-conflict-latest-news-liveblog-ws-kl-10377565.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
