       <h1>Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman Relocates Amid Rising Houthi Attacks</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman is reportedly being moved between heavily guarded palaces equipped with bunkers as Houthi rebel missile attacks intensify. The prince, who has not appeared in public since Tuesday, is protected by a handpicked security team while the kingdom faces repeated threats to strategic infrastructure.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/saudi-crown-prince-mohammed-bin-salman-relocates-amid-rising.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Houthi forces have targeted airports, oil refineries, and pipelines, complicating Saudi economic diversification plans. Recent attacks included a ballistic missile strike near a medical complex in Riyadh. Saudi officials are currently seeking additional international military assistance to bolster defenses as the kingdom reports a dwindling supply of missile interceptors.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the security situation but misses the source's detail that the Crown Prince donated blood on Tuesday, which provides context for his recent public absence.</p>
