       <h1>The Survival Gap: Why India’s Breast Cancer Survival Trails the World</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Breast Cancer</span> <span>#Health</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>During Breast Cancer Awareness Month, ETHealthworld is examining the reasons behind India’s breast cancer survival rate remaining below the global median. This initiative highlights a critical health disparity.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/the-survival-gap-why-indias-breast-cancer-survival-trails-th.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The analysis focuses on identifying the existing gaps in early detection and screening processes across the country. Addressing these deficiencies is crucial for improving patient outcomes.</p><p>Furthermore, the report will include insights from doctors regarding the necessary changes needed to enhance breast cancer survival rates in India. Their perspectives will outline key interventions and policy adjustments.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the scope and intent of the ETHealthworld report as described in the source summary.</p>
