       <h1>Tips to Improve iPhone Camera Performance and Reduce Blurry Photos</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Blurry iPhone photography is frequently caused by external factors like smudged lenses or poor lighting rather than software failure. Users should clean lenses with a microfiber cloth—using distilled water if marks persist—and ensure settings are adjusted for high-resolution output above 720p.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/tips-to-improve-iphone-camera-performance-and-reduce-blurry-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>To further improve image clarity, users should manage low-light conditions which often force slower shutter speeds and introduce grain. Activating Night Mode in dim environments or utilizing AE/AF lock by tapping and holding the screen can stabilize focus, preventing the camera from shifting unexpectedly and helping capture sharper, higher-quality images.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Provides actionable advice from the source while correctly attributing the camera settings and maintenance tips.</p>
