     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-12 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>VFS Global May Launch ‘Study in India’ Product, Says Zubin Karkaria</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#VFS Global</span> <span>#Study in India</span> <span>#International Students</span> <span>#Education</span></div>
       <p>Zubin Karkaria, as reported by The Economic Times, has indicated that VFS Global is considering the launch of a new ‘Study in India’ product. This initiative aims to enhance India's appeal as an educational destination.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-12/vfs-global-may-launch-study-in-india-product-says-zubin-kark.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The proposed product by VFS Global would specifically target and attract international students. The goal is to streamline the process for foreign nationals wishing to pursue their education in India.</p><p>This move could potentially simplify visa and related services, making it easier for students globally to access Indian educational institutions.</p><p>What to watch: Further announcements on the launch and features of the ‘Study in India’ product.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting based on the provided summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
